WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.590
COLT MCANLIS: Google
Cloud Next 2017

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.980
has hosted a plethora of talks
detailing the future of cloud.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.100
If you didn't get a chance to
check out Mete Atamel's talk,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.920
"Running .NET on Google
Cloud," then stay tuned

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.970
because here's the recap.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.041
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:19.940
RETO MEIER: Historically,
.NET and Google Cloud Platform

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.002
haven't exactly
played well together.

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:23.960
COLT MCANLIS: The reasons
for this are complex,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.460
and one of the
biggest challenges

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.790
has been around the language and
tooling not working very well

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.047
with scalable Linux VMs.

00:00:30.047 --> 00:00:30.755
RETO MEIER: But--

00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:31.610
COLT MCANLIS: Brace yourselves.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.650
RETO MEIER: --that's
no longer the case.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.900
COLT MCANLIS: Improved
Linux support for the .NET

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.870
environment has allowed the
framework to extend its reach.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.200
And the availability of Windows
VMs on Google Compute Engine

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.330
opens doors for new
types of applications

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.310
to run on Google infrastructure.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.430
See, the decision to run .NET
on GCP is no longer an issue

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.810
of features and support.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:54.110
It's about choosing the best
cloud platform for your needs.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.910
And when it comes
to .NET development,

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.150
GCP has some new features to
help you be more productive.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.710
RETO MEIER: Let's
start by looking

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.030
at the libraries and tools.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.430
We've provided a suite
of runtime libraries

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.230
that make it easy
for your application

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.770
to interface with the full
suite of GCP services.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.780
That includes everything
from the Vision API,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.050
Natural Speech API,
Authentication, and Datastore,

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.590
all available for your .NET app.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.420
We're also providing Visual
Studio plugins and PowerShell

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.180
cmdlets to help you
manage your GCP resources

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.430
from within the tools you're
already using on a day

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.477
to day basis.

00:01:26.477 --> 00:01:28.310
COLT MCANLIS: On the
compute side of things,

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.950
we've got support to boot
a VM with Windows on it.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.000
But we also go further by
offering Google Cloud Launcher,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.370
which gives you one quick
deployment to Windows servers

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.950
that come pre-installed
with things like ASP.NET

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.190
and the Google Cloud
Platform .NET libraries.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.040
But if you've already done
that legwork yourself and are

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.640
running say, a container with
Windows and ASP.NET Core on it,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.610
don't fret.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.460
You can deploy that
with ease using

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.300
App Engine Flex environment or
our Kubernetes platform, Google

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.459
Container Engine.

00:01:57.459 --> 00:01:59.000
And the best part
is that all of this

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.670
is running on Google's
infrastructure, which already

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.700
offers fast VM provisioning,
simple autoscaling,

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.820
and per minute billing,
not to mention access

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.090
to managed services like
BigTable, Datastore, Dataflow,

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.610
cloud storage, and
genomics processing.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.040
RETO MEIER: GCP also
provides a federation

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.440
of tools and services
which make your deployments

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.700
production-ready.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.920
The health check system
can monitor your instances,

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.070
and a fully expanded and
accessible orphaned IM system

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.120
allows you to control who and
what has access to everything.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.820
And plus there's integration
to Stackdriver, which gives you

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.310
logging, reporting, tracing,
and monitoring of your cloud

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.739
service, right out of the box.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.280
COLT MCANLIS: Check
out the recording

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.480
of Mete's full session to see a
bunch of cool demos of ASP.NET

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.070
running on Google Cloud.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.230
And if you want more recaps
on great Next content,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.230
make sure to check out
the rest of the playlist.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.650
And don't forget the Next world
tour, which is coming soon

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.790
to a city near you.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.140
[MUSIC PLAYING]

